{
  "id": "CA-AB-1135-2016",
  "scope": "state:ca",
  "title": "AB 1135 (Levine) (2015-16) — Bullet-button / easily changeable magazine rule for military-style assault weapons (class ban expansion)",
  "urls": [
    "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billVotesClient.xhtml?bill_id=201520160AB1135 (403 via WebFetch and curl)",
    "Lead pages from search, not fetched: https://www.leginfo.ca.gov/pub/15-16/bill/asm/ab_1101-1150/ab_1135_bill_20160701_history.html ; https://legiscan.com/CA/rollcall/AB1135/id/556724"
  ],
  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "Section 30515 (Penal Code): (a) Notwithstanding Section 30510, \"assault weapon\" also means any of the following:\nSection 30515 (Penal Code): (a)(1) A semiautomatic, centerfire rifle that does not have a fixed magazine but has any one of the following: (A) A pistol grip that protrudes conspicuously beneath the action of the weapon. (B) A thumbhole stock. (C) A folding or telescoping stock. (D) A grenade launcher or flare launcher. (E) A flash suppressor. (F) A forward pistol grip.\nSection 30515 (Penal Code): (a)(2) A semiautomatic, centerfire rifle that has a fixed magazine with the capacity to accept more than 10 rounds.\nSection 30515 (Penal Code): (a)(5) A semiautomatic pistol with a fixed magazine that has the capacity to accept more than 10 rounds.\nSection 30515 (Penal Code): (a)(8) Any shotgun with a revolving cylinder.\nSection 30680 (Penal Code): Section 30605 does not apply to the possession of an assault weapon by a person who has possessed the assault weapon prior to January 1, 2017, if all of the following are applicable:\nSection 30680 (Penal Code): (c) The person registers the assault weapon by January 1, 2018, in accordance with subdivision (b) of Section 30900.\nSection 30900 (Penal Code): (b) (1) Any person who, from January 1, 2001, to December 31, 2016, inclusive, lawfully possessed an assault weapon that does not have a fixed magazine, as defined in Section 30515, including those weapons with an ammunition feeding device that can be readily removed from the firearm with the use of a tool, shall register the firearm before January 1, 2018, but not before the effective date of the regulations adopted pursuant to paragraph (5), with the department pursuant to those procedures that the department may establish by regulation pursuant to paragraph (5).",
